---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, AUTHOR_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Kseniia"
  description="About Rumroom World — practical, researched travel guides for slow travelers and digital nomads, and how the site makes money."
>
  <div class="container-main py-20">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h1 class="font-display text-5xl font-bold text-primary mb-4">About</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-primary/70 italic mb-12">
        A quick look at what this blog is, who writes it, and how it's put together.
      </p>

      <div class="prose-article">
        <!-- Author intro card -->
        <div class="bg-soft/5 border border-soft/20 rounded-lg p-8 mb-12">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-6 flex-col sm:flex-row">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0">
              <div
                class="w-32 h-32 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-400 via-teal-500 to-cyan-600 flex items-center justify-center text-6xl drop-shadow-lg"
                aria-label="Kseniia avatar placeholder"
              >
                <span aria-hidden="true">🌴</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-primary mb-3">
                Hi, I'm Kseniia 👋
              </h2>
              <p class="text-primary/80">
                I run Rumroom World — practical, researched guides for slow travel and remote work, without sponsored fluff or Instagram bait.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-primary mt-12 mb-4">Who this is for</h2>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-6">
          If you're a <strong>slow traveler</strong> — someone who'd rather spend a month in one neighborhood than tick off six countries in a fortnight — or a <strong>digital nomad</strong> figuring out where to actually base yourself this season, this blog is for you. It's written especially with women travelers and remote workers in mind.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-primary mt-12 mb-4">What this site covers</h2>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-4">
          Practical, honest guides — not destination listicles. The kind of stuff that helps you make the next decision:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-primary/80 mb-6 space-y-2">
          <li>🛂 Visa logistics — what's actually possible vs. what travel agents oversell</li>
          <li>🏡 Where to live for 1-6 months — neighborhoods, not just cities</li>
          <li>💸 Real cost of living — researched numbers, not Reddit estimates from 2018</li>
          <li>💻 Coworking, wifi, and remote-work realities — including which "digital nomad hubs" are overrated</li>
          <li>🛵 Getting around — scooters, transfers, when to walk</li>
          <li>🍜 Where to eat — local picks, not Instagram traps</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-6">
          Right now the deepest coverage is on <a href="/pillars/bali/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-semibold">Bali</a>, with growing guides for France and Italy.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-primary mt-12 mb-4">Why "Rumroom"?</h2>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-6">
          The name comes from the idea of "room for thoughts" — a small, quiet space to think clearly. It's the same brand behind a marketing blog at <a href="https://rumroom.space" class="text-accent hover:underline">rumroom.space</a> and an older Russian-language version at travel.rumroom.ru.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-primary mt-12 mb-4">How this site makes money (honest version)</h2>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-4">
          Some of the links in these guides — for things like travel insurance, eSIMs, scooter rentals, accommodation, and visa services — are <strong>affiliate links</strong>. That means if you click one and end up booking, this site gets a small commission. <strong>It doesn't cost you anything extra.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-4">
          What this site will <em>never</em> do:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-primary/80 mb-6 space-y-2">
          <li>✅ Recommend a service without researching it first</li>
          <li>✅ Take money to write about a place or product</li>
          <li>✅ Hide the fact that a link is affiliate</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-6">
          Full disclosure on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/" class="text-accent hover:underline font-semibold">Affiliate Disclosure page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-primary mt-12 mb-4">A note on AI</h2>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-6">
          AI tools are used here to help with translation (between Russian and English), research scaffolding, and editing. Every guide is fact-checked and reviewed before publishing. If something looks off, get in touch and it'll get corrected.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-primary mt-12 mb-4">Get in touch</h2>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-3">
          Got a question, a correction, or want a recommendation that hasn't been written up yet? Every email gets read.
        </p>
        <p class="text-primary/80 mb-2">
          📧 <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR_EMAIL}`} class="text-accent font-semibold hover:underline">
            {AUTHOR_EMAIL}
          </a>
        </p>
        <p class="text-primary/60 text-sm italic mt-8">
          Thanks for reading. — Kseniia
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
